      {
        "title": {
          "en": "Microsoft Research Introduces Generative Causal Testing for Brain Understanding",
          "zh": "微软研究院推出生成式因果测试以理解大脑"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "Microsoft researchers introduced generative causal testing, a method to translate black box models into clear hypotheses and verify them to identify brain regions responding to language.",
          "zh": "微软研究人员引入了生成式因果测试，该方法可将黑盒模型转化为清晰的假设并在扫描仪中验证，以揭示特定大脑区域对语言的反应。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "Researchers at Microsoft introduced 'generative causal testing'.",
            "This method translates 'black box models' into clear hypotheses.",
            "Hypotheses are verified in a scanner to identify specific brain regions that respond to language."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "微软研究人员引入了“生成式因果测试”。",
            "该方法可将“黑盒模型”转化为清晰的假设。",
            "假设在扫描仪中得到验证，以识别对语言有反应的特定大脑区域。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This research provides a method to demystify black box AI models by translating their outputs into testable hypotheses for brain activity. It offers a new approach for understanding how the brain processes language, bridging AI interpretation and neuroscience.",
          "zh": "这项研究提供了一种通过将黑盒AI模型的输出转化为可测试的大脑活动假设来揭示其内部机制的方法。它为理解大脑如何处理语言提供了一种新途径，连接了AI解释与神经科学。"
        },
        "source": "Microsoft Research",
